Description: Wi-Fi page in the on-screen settings menu (NetworkManager/nmcli)
 The XDJ400 has no keyboard and no desktop: joining a new Wi-Fi network
 meant an ssh session, which needs the network you are trying to join. The
 settings menu (cog) gains a WI-FI entry that opens a full-screen page:
 connection status with IP address, the networks in range (strongest
 first, one row per SSID, CONNECTED / SAVED / OPEN / ENTERPRISE tags),
 RESCAN and paging. Tapping a network connects -- straight away for open
 and saved ones, via a password page for new secured ones. Tapping the
 connected network arms "TAP AGAIN TO FORGET", the same tap-again-to-
 confirm the menu's POWER OFF uses.
 .
 New widget WWifiPanel (src/widget/wwifipanel.{h,cpp}, skin tag
 <WifiPanel>) holds the dynamic part: it drives NetworkManager through
 nmcli, always asynchronously (a scan takes seconds and the GUI thread
 must never wait on it), retrying through passwordless sudo when polkit
 refuses the session. Everything around it -- BACK, RESCAN, PREV/NEXT,
 the keyboard -- is ordinary skin buttons pressing [Library],wifi_*
 controls that LibraryControl forwards to the bound panel, exactly how
 the search box receives the search keyboard. wifi_page / wifi_entry are
 the two state controls the skin reads (page shown; password entry open,
 so the keyboard is up). menu_disarm (cog, scrim, BACK) also closes the
 page, so the menu always reopens on its main screen.
 .
 The on-screen keyboard is generalised for this: setupOnScreenKeyboard()
 creates one control set per prefix ("search", "wifi"), and both gain a
 one-shot shift latch and a punctuation layer (<prefix>_key_c<codepoint>,
 since the characters themselves cannot name a control) -- a Wi-Fi
 password needs capitals and symbols, a track search does not mind them.
 search_clear joins clear_search so keyboard.xml can be one template.
